1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,879
[GROANING, GRUNTING]

2
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:06,798
[BILLY]
<i>What happened to you?</i>

3
00:00:06,881 --> 00:00:08,299
<i>Why did you</i>
<i>suddenly snap?</i>

4
00:00:08,383 --> 00:00:10,301
<i>You're right.</i>
<i>I snapped.</i>

5
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:12,303
<i>I was reminded of my dad.</i>

6
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:14,681
<i>I couldn't protect her from Dad.</i>

7
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:16,349
<i>But now, things are different.</i>

8
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:19,436
<i>- To freedom!</i>
<i>- To freedom!</i>

9
00:00:19,519 --> 00:00:20,812
[MARJ] <i>Real friends don't snitch.</i>

10
00:00:20,895 --> 00:00:23,189
<i>I dare you to show</i>
<i>your messages and calls.</i>

11
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,149
[CHARM] <i>That's right.</i>

12
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:25,066
[GROANS]

13
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,944
[ABI] <i>Caloy! Why did you come straight</i>
<i>here? What if someone followed you?</i>

14
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:31,573
<i>How can you be sure</i>
<i>the taxi driver is telling the truth?</i>

15
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:34,534
<i>This taxi driver</i>
<i>is our best shot right now.</i>

16
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:37,871
<i>He's our only lead to the woman</i>
<i>who gave him the money.</i>

17
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:40,623
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

18
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:43,334
I only told you to scare
the driver, right?

19
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:44,627
The driver.

20
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:47,756
You involved Jordan.
Now look what's happened.

21
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:51,342
How was I to know that Jordan
would also be there?

22
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:53,470
Did I know that, huh?

23
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:55,263
I didn't know, okay?

24
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:56,556
But here, look.

25
00:00:57,390 --> 00:01:00,560
Now take a look at this.

26
00:01:00,643 --> 00:01:02,312
Look, 'Bi!

27
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,981
LOVELIST'S JORDAN VALENTIN
INVOLVED IN ASSAULT.

28
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,484
We don't need trolls anymore.

29
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:11,404
The netizens themselves will
now shred him to pieces.

30
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:14,240
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

31
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:16,451
- THIS IS DANGEROUS BEHAVIOR.
- TALK FIRST BEFORE FIGHTING.

32
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:17,869
Is that nice?

33
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:22,874
Caloy, you can't always
act like that, okay?

34
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:26,795
Things can't always be this way.
Especially now, Caloy!

35
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:31,883
Not now that I'm finally
getting close to my idol.

36
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:35,929
What if they find out that
we have a connection?

37
00:01:36,721 --> 00:01:38,014
[CALOY] Why?

38
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:39,265
Are you close already?

39
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:40,850
Did you get inside their company already?

40
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:44,270
Not yet! How could that happen?

41
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:48,399
If Billy and Jordan go harder after you,

42
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,026
we're going to be in a tight spot!

43
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,319
That's my point.

44
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:53,947
That's why I can't do that.

45
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:55,031
My goodness, Caloy!

46
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:58,743
I can already imagine it.

47
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:01,746
Her friends would invite me out.

48
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:04,249
"Hey, Abi! Let's have a drink."

49
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:06,835
"Abi, I love you!"

50
00:02:06,918 --> 00:02:09,963
"Cheers! Let's take a shot!"

51
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:12,340
"It's so fun hanging out with you, Abi!"

52
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:15,510
You know, like,
I'd be hanging out with her friends too!

53
00:02:15,593 --> 00:02:17,637
I'd get invited to events.

54
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:19,973
I'd attend an awards night.

55
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:21,474
And then…

56
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:26,271
I want to get on stage,
accept an award, and give a speech.

57
00:02:26,354 --> 00:02:28,690
"Thank you so much.
This is for you, Caloy."

58
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:30,525
And then everyone would applaud!

59
00:02:30,608 --> 00:02:33,278
"Thank you. Thank you.
I love you all so much."

60
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:35,321
"You inspire me."

61
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,532
That's what I want, Caloy.

62
00:02:37,615 --> 00:02:39,159
Don't worry.

63
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:41,870
Everything you said will happen.

64
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:43,204
I promise you that.

65
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:47,876
Besides, Jordan's already in jail.

66
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:51,212
- We're so close to--
- He was in jail.

67
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:52,547
Yes, he was.

68
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,882
But now, he's free.

69
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:57,093
His friend just posted
that he was released.

70
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,887
What?

71
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:00,346
H-how?

72
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:03,349
I have no idea. How would I know?

73
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:04,976
That's what I'm saying, Caloy.

74
00:03:05,059 --> 00:03:07,687
We can't do things carelessly.

75
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:11,024
Do you know what'll happen
if we get caught?

76
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:13,151
You'll go back to prison again.

77
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:16,237
I'll finish the job. Wait a second.

78
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:18,573
Oh, calm down! Calm down.

79
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:21,159
- I'll go--
- Calm down!

80
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:23,036
I'll go to that man!

81
00:03:23,119 --> 00:03:25,330
[CALOY RETCHING]

82
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:27,749
Go on. Go to him and vomit.

83
00:03:27,832 --> 00:03:31,336
[GRUNTING]

84
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:36,049
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:38,218
[VALERIE] Okay, fine!

86
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:41,554
It's…

87
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:44,057
[MUMBLING]
one, four, three, Jordan.

88
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,391
- What?
- Huh?

89
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:46,643
[JORDAN] What?

90
00:03:48,102 --> 00:03:49,312
One, four, three, Jordan.

91
00:03:49,395 --> 00:03:51,397
One, four, three, Jordan?

92
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:55,151
As in, "I love you, Jordan?"

93
00:03:55,735 --> 00:03:57,195
It could also mean…

94
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:59,447
"I hate you, Jordan."

95
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:00,865
- Check it already.
- Really?

96
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:02,575
Well? Is it okay now?

97
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:04,869
I can't see anything.

98
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:05,995
Well, sorry then.

99
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:08,373
Okay, give me my phone back.

100
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:09,874
What is this?

101
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:12,168
- What is it?
- What, did you find any evidence?

102
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:14,045
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:04:14,128 --> 00:04:15,797
"5:00 p.m."?

104
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:18,383
"See you…

105
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:22,095
at Le Jardin Hotel?"

106
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,846
That's a five-star hotel.

107
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:25,223
You wouldn't…

108
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,351
even take me to a motel.

109
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:30,436
There are even cute emojis here!

110
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:33,481
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

111
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:35,400
Love, let me explain--

112
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:36,818
[GASPS]

113
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:39,153
- You witch!
- [SCREAMING]

114
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:41,864
- Stop! No!
- Calm down!

115
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:45,535
You're going after my boyfriend
after being done with Jordan?!

116
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:47,662
- Billy, get her out of here!
- Stop! That's enough!

117
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:49,872
- Let him explain first!
- Go, Toni!

118
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:52,583
- That's enough!
- Wait, stop!

119
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:56,337
- Get that woman out of here!
- Stop! Enough!

120
00:04:56,421 --> 00:04:59,048
- Wait, calm down first!
- Hey, stop texting my man!

121
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:05,847
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:43,968
Yani.

123
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:47,930
What is the truth?
Why were you talking with Val?

124
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:52,602
Answer her!

125
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:53,811
It's…

126
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:57,356
This is why. Here.

127
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,025
[YANI GRUNTS]

128
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:02,320
I was asking her to help me
propose to you.

129
00:06:02,403 --> 00:06:04,906
Why didn't you just say so right away?

130
00:06:04,989 --> 00:06:06,657
Why would I?

131
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:08,785
It's a secret. A surprise.

132
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:14,040
Yani, it's just that out of everyone,
why did you ask Valerie for help?

133
00:06:14,123 --> 00:06:15,541
[MARJ] We're right here.

134
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:20,004
Because she has a contact
at the Le Jardin Hotel.

135
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:23,341
They have a beautiful garden there, right?
An overlook with a view.

136
00:06:24,342 --> 00:06:26,969
It's the perfect spot for a proposal.

137
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:30,807
I manage all of
their social media accounts,

138
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:34,769
so I told Yani that
I'd help him get a discount.

139
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:38,898
I'm sorry, Val.

140
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,486
We were mistaken.

141
00:06:44,862 --> 00:06:46,405
We're very sorry.

142
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:50,660
I just wanted to help Yani.

143
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:55,456
And I wanted you girls
to know I'm on your side.

144
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:57,708
I just wanted to be friends with you,

145
00:06:57,792 --> 00:07:00,837
even if we're not on the same level.

146
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,046
What?

147
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:03,422
Mm.

148
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:05,216
[WHISPERS] Easy.

149
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:09,345
[CHARM CLEARS THROAT]

150
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:10,972
Sorry.

151
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:13,349
I'm sorry too.

152
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,184
I messed up big time.

153
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:18,271
But, love…

154
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:23,151
why did your proposal
have to be so extravagant?

155
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:26,070
Well, you're always comparing me to Ralph.

156
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,490
Sometimes, you'd even say,

157
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:34,412
"Hey, Yani, did you know
Ralph took Charm to Boracay?"

158
00:07:34,495 --> 00:07:35,663
"They had a vacation there."

159
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:39,292
"And did you know
they eat at Charcoal Haven?"

160
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:41,878
"They probably go there all the time
because it's so good."

161
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:43,921
"They also go to this place too.
It must be really nice--"

162
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:44,922
Sorry.

163
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:49,760
I never meant to make you feel…

164
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:52,096
That's why I did all this.

165
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:55,224
Just so I could make it up to you.

166
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:57,185
At least with the proposal,

167
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:59,312
I wanted you to see me as someone better.

168
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:00,980
I love you.

169
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:06,027
Even if you're just a struggling painter.

170
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:08,821
I love you even if you're sensitive.

171
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:13,117
I love you even if
you only take me to Dolomite Beach.

172
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:17,663
I love you even if we only eat
at a local beef stew joint.

173
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:21,125
You'll still love him

174
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:24,337
even if he doesn't propose
at Le Jardin Hotel?

175
00:08:25,796 --> 00:08:26,964
What?

176
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:29,926
Well, now that it's out,

177
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:32,345
I think this is the perfect time.

178
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,096
Yans.

179
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:36,516
Did you prepare your proposal speech?

180
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:38,434
- Ready?
- Of course.

181
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:39,602
There you go.

182
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:40,895
What are we waiting for?

183
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:42,563
- Go, go, go!
- [CLAPPING]

184
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:44,106
Oh my God, girl!

185
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:46,192
- [YANI CLEARS THROAT]
- [JORDAN] Go, brother.

186
00:08:46,275 --> 00:08:48,361
- This is it, girl.
- Go, go, go!

187
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:53,449
Love, may I have your hand?

188
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:59,580
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:04,460
You're the inspiration
behind all my dreams.

190
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:06,379
That's why I never give up.

191
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:09,131
I love you so much.

192
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,510
My muse…

193
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:15,221
Antonia Prieto.

194
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,349
Will you marry me?

195
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:21,060
Yes.

196
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:22,436
- [SQUEALING]
- [APPLAUSE]

197
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,105
- Oh my God!
- Yes!

198
00:09:24,188 --> 00:09:26,566
- Oh my God!
- Congrats!

199
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:28,192
Yes!

200
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:30,570
- Congratulations!
- [ROBBIE] Go, Yani!

201
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:32,613
[APPLAUSE]

202
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:36,826
- [ROBBIE] Go Yani!
- [BLAIRE] When will our turn come?

203
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:39,287
- [BLAIRE] What about us?
- [YANI] That's true!

204
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:40,871
Thank you.

205
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,415
- I'm heading home.
- Hmm.

206
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:43,583
Home?

207
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:45,334
Can you even make it home?

208
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:46,877
I don't think you can.

209
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:48,212
Just stay here.

210
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,755
Sleep here tonight.

211
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:52,300
Thank you.

212
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:54,677
And I'm sorry.

213
00:09:57,138 --> 00:10:01,892
Caloy, who is going to have our backs
if not each other?

214
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:03,686
Just friends?

215
00:10:04,186 --> 00:10:06,105
Want me to add another bruise?

216
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:07,773
This time on the other side?

217
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,400
'Bi, I'm serious.

218
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:10,568
Hmm.

219
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:12,987
You've always been there for me.

220
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,740
If it weren't for you,

221
00:10:17,491 --> 00:10:19,368
I probably wouldn't even be here.

222
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:23,289
- [BLADE SWISHES]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

223
00:10:23,372 --> 00:10:25,458
<i>- Come on! Come on!</i>
- [CALOY GRUNTING]

224
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:28,419
<i>Bastards!</i>

225
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:32,298
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

226
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:34,133
<i>Help! Help! Hold on!</i>

227
00:10:34,216 --> 00:10:36,344
<i>Take me to the hospital!</i>
[GRUNTS] <i>It hurts!</i>

228
00:10:36,427 --> 00:10:38,012
[HORN HONKING]

229
00:10:38,095 --> 00:10:39,597
<i>Sir, help me, please.</i>

230
00:10:41,098 --> 00:10:42,725
[CALOY GRUNTING]

231
00:10:42,808 --> 00:10:43,768
<i>What happened?</i>

232
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:45,478
<i>Oh, there's blood!</i>

233
00:10:45,561 --> 00:10:48,022
<i>Sir? Hey! Are you okay? Hey!</i>

234
00:10:48,105 --> 00:10:49,315
<i>Help! Help!</i>

235
00:10:49,398 --> 00:10:50,900
<i>Oh! That looks pretty deep.</i>

236
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:53,194
<i>What, are you all deaf? Help!</i>

237
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,403
<i>Tricycle!</i>

238
00:10:54,487 --> 00:10:56,030
<i>What happened to you?</i>

239
00:10:56,113 --> 00:10:58,032
<i>Oh my God!</i>
<i>Get in!</i>

240
00:10:58,115 --> 00:10:59,742
<i>To the nearest hospital, please!</i>

241
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:00,660
<i>Let's go, hurry!</i>

242
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:02,745
Caloy, if I'd known
you'd just come from a fight,

243
00:11:02,828 --> 00:11:04,372
I might not have helped you.

244
00:11:04,455 --> 00:11:05,706
Just stay here.

245
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:08,084
Come on.

246
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:09,710
Lie down. Get some rest.

247
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:12,088
So I can head home too.

248
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,885
My parents disowned me.

249
00:11:17,968 --> 00:11:21,639
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

250
00:11:21,722 --> 00:11:23,849
But you, someone I'm not even related to…

251
00:11:26,143 --> 00:11:27,895
have always been by my side.

252
00:11:30,689 --> 00:11:32,525
Caloy, we're the same, aren't we?

253
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:35,486
Our parents both abandoned us.

254
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:41,450
That's why we're all we've got.

255
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,412
So I hope you understand

256
00:11:46,288 --> 00:11:48,666
why we need to keep our distance for now.

257
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:50,835
It's for our own good.

258
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,796
We have to be even more careful.

259
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:57,049
Anything for you, Bea.

260
00:11:59,009 --> 00:12:00,469
What did you say?

261
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:02,721
Bea.

262
00:12:02,805 --> 00:12:04,390
What did you say?!

263
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:06,183
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

264
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:07,101
[MUTTERS] Abi.

265
00:12:07,184 --> 00:12:08,436
Hmm?

266
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:09,812
[LOUDER] Abi.

267
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:11,564
Get some rest.

268
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:16,527
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:17,653
[THUDS]

270
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:23,701
[BILLY] <i>Love gives second chances</i>
<i>to those who deserve it.</i>

271
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:26,537
<i>And these women are proof of that.</i>

272
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,247
<i>I believe that</i>

273
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:31,709
<i>love should only</i>
<i>be given to the right person.</i>

274
00:12:33,752 --> 00:12:36,922
<i>And yes, there are still a lot</i>
<i>of good people out there.</i>

275
00:12:37,006 --> 00:12:39,800
<i>That's why LoveList,</i>
<i>a matchmaking and dating app,</i>

276
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:41,969
<i>- is here for you.</i>
- [PHONE CHIMES]

277
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:45,514
<i>But we created not just an application,</i>

278
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:49,185
<i>but a community of women who work together</i>

279
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:52,146
<i>to help you find "the one."</i>
<i>Because I believe…</i>

280
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:54,064
PAY BY MONTH'S END,
OR I'LL PADLOCK YOUR UNIT.

281
00:12:54,148 --> 00:12:56,650
<i>…that love is supposed to be</i>
<i>the most beautiful thing</i>

282
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:58,068
<i>that can happen to you.</i>

283
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:00,863
<i>As long as it is with the right one.</i>

284
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:03,407
[PARTY GUESTS IN UNISON IN VIDEO]
<i>At the right time!</i>

285
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:04,700
[BILLY] <i>And fun fact,</i>

286
00:13:04,783 --> 00:13:06,118
<i>Toni and Charm…</i>

287
00:13:06,202 --> 00:13:08,162
[ABI]<i> I can already imagine it.</i>

288
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:11,123
<i>Her friends would invite me out.</i>

289
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:13,626
<i>"Hey, Abi! Let's have a drink."</i>

290
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:16,795
<i>You know, like,</i>
<i>I'd be hanging out with her friends too!</i>

291
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:19,048
<i>I'd get invited to events.</i>

292
00:13:19,131 --> 00:13:21,383
<i>I'd attend an awards night.</i>

293
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:22,885
<i>And then…</i>

294
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:28,224
<i>I want to get on stage, accept</i>
<i>an award, and give a speech.</i>

295
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:38,359
[UTENSIL CLANKS]

296
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:43,614
You're already home late,
and this is what you bring me?

297
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,366
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

298
00:13:45,449 --> 00:13:46,575
What kind of soup is this?

299
00:13:46,659 --> 00:13:47,868
It's cold!

300
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:51,205
Then I'll just heat it up.

301
00:13:51,288 --> 00:13:53,123
- [SLAMS]
- I've lost my appetite!

302
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:57,086
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

303
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:58,379
Are you hurt?

304
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:00,130
No.

305
00:14:02,716 --> 00:14:04,134
Here. You can have it.

306
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:08,055
No, thanks.
I've lost my appetite too.

307
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:10,808
I'll reheat it.

308
00:14:10,891 --> 00:14:12,434
Don't bother.

309
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:15,813
Don't bother. I got it.

310
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,147
I'll do it.

311
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:23,320
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

312
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:29,034
Daughter?

313
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:30,786
Sorry.

314
00:14:32,746 --> 00:14:33,998
It's okay.

315
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:36,375
[PLATE CLINKS]

316
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:39,253
[CLATTERING]

317
00:14:39,336 --> 00:14:45,509
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:54,018
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

319
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:55,185
- Hey.
- Hmm?

320
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:56,353
[PHONE CHIMES]

321
00:14:56,437 --> 00:14:57,980
BIBOY'S FATHER
FILED ANOTHER COMPLAINT!

322
00:14:58,063 --> 00:14:59,690
Please don't look at the comments.

323
00:15:00,441 --> 00:15:02,735
If you want, we can take legal action

324
00:15:02,818 --> 00:15:05,404
to stop the video from spreading further.

325
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:07,489
This is different.

326
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:09,283
- What is that?
- Mm.

327
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:11,493
Nothing. I got it.

328
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,954
Could you just get me
another drink, please?

329
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:15,998
You're driving, remember?

330
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:18,000
I'm perfectly fine.

331
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:19,835
- Look. Yes.
- Are you sure?

332
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:22,880
Thank you.

333
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:30,304
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:31,388
What is going on?

335
00:15:31,472 --> 00:15:32,806
- There you go again!
- What is it?

336
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:34,350
Is it your dad?

337
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:37,811
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

338
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,521
<i>Jordan is okay now.</i>

339
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:41,649
<i>But what we're not okay with</i>

340
00:15:41,732 --> 00:15:45,152
<i>is how we still can't track down</i>
<i>the mastermind behind this.</i>

341
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:47,821
WELCOME TO
THE PHILIPPINES!

342
00:15:49,823 --> 00:15:53,577
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

343
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:56,914
[BUSY TONE]

344
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,251
[GIRL] Daddy!

345
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:02,628
Daddy!

346
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:04,964
[GIRL GUSHING]

347
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:11,929
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

348
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:21,605
There you go again.

349
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:24,483
You're making my problems
your responsibility.

350
00:16:25,275 --> 00:16:26,276
Mm!

351
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:30,906
Why don't we talk about
how you ended up in jail?

352
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:32,783
- I'd rather not.
- Come on.

353
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:33,701
Go.

354
00:16:34,868 --> 00:16:36,620
[BILLY CLEARS THROAT]

355
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:37,746
I'm sorry about that.

356
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:42,167
Are you really okay?

357
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:48,632
[FRIENDS] Kiss! Come on!
[CHEERING, CLAPPING]

358
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:50,342
- [BILLY CHUCKLES]
- [CHEERING]

359
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:52,803
- Whoo!
- [YANI] Let's go! Cheers!

360
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:55,305
- [FRIENDS] Cheers!
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

361
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:56,390
What about you?

362
00:16:56,974 --> 00:16:58,392
Are you really okay?

363
00:16:59,768 --> 00:17:03,022
Why do you keep asking me that?
You're like a broken record!

364
00:17:03,105 --> 00:17:04,440
- I'm fine!
- Okay!

365
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:06,316
- Let's dance.
- Okay!

366
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,485
- Okay.
- Jordan wants to dance!

367
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,946
[CHEERING]

368
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:16,785
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

369
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:21,415
[MUSIC FADES]

370
00:17:24,084 --> 00:17:25,502
It's turned red.

371
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:28,130
This'll definitely bruise by tomorrow.

372
00:17:30,841 --> 00:17:31,967
So annoying.

373
00:17:33,552 --> 00:17:34,970
[SIGHS]

374
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:38,974
I'm okay.

375
00:17:40,225 --> 00:17:41,852
Hi, Ms. Billy.

376
00:17:43,645 --> 00:17:45,105
Idol.

377
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:49,568
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

378
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:50,527
There.

379
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,154
My newly-printed pictures.

380
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:55,699
I have another addition to my collection.

381
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,663
You're so beautiful here.

382
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,088
[LIGHT SWITCH CLICKS]

383
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:15,969
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

384
00:18:20,974 --> 00:18:22,476
[SQUEALS]

385
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:26,730
[SIGHS]

386
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:30,400
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:31,401
[PHONE CHIMES]

388
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:41,870
<i>Whoo! LFG!</i>

389
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:45,499
- <i>Whoo! Let's go!</i>
- [PEOPLE CHEERING]

390
00:18:45,582 --> 00:18:47,960
<i>Congratulations for Yani and Toni!</i>

391
00:18:48,043 --> 00:18:50,170
<i>- Whoo!</i>
<i>- Congrats!</i>

392
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:57,010
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER,
CHEERING ON VIDEO]

393
00:18:57,094 --> 00:18:58,720
Cheers!

394
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:00,389
Whoo!

395
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:02,516
Cheers!

396
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:04,393
[PEOPLE CHEERING ON VIDEO]

397
00:19:04,476 --> 00:19:10,774
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

398
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:19,867
- Whoo! Cheers!
- [CHEERING ON VIDEO]

399
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:21,785
- [TONI] <i>Go Billy!</i>
- [MARJ] <i>Lower!</i>

400
00:19:21,869 --> 00:19:22,911
[MARJ] <i>Go lower!</i>

401
00:19:22,995 --> 00:19:27,833
[CHANTING] <i>Lower! Lower! Lower! Lower!</i>

402
00:19:27,916 --> 00:19:30,794
- <i>Lower! Lower!</i>
- [CHEERING]

403
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:33,005
[HEELS THUD]

404
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:36,258
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:39,469
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [ENGINES REVVING]

406
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:45,309
Bye! Take care! [CHUCKLES]

407
00:19:49,563 --> 00:19:51,732
- [CAR DOOR CLOSES]
- [ENGINE STARTS]

408
00:19:58,614 --> 00:20:03,118
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:06,246
[PHONE RINGING]

410
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:08,624
Hello?

411
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:10,000
Hello?

412
00:20:11,418 --> 00:20:13,879
Benilda? Sweetie?

413
00:20:13,962 --> 00:20:17,174
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

414
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:19,426
[LINE DISCONNECTING]

415
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:33,607
Billy, why do you think
he suddenly called you?

416
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:36,485
After-- How many? Um…

417
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:40,405
More than ten years, right?

418
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:43,242
I don't know either.

419
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,494
Don't you think you should find out why?

420
00:20:45,577 --> 00:20:51,708
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

421
00:20:51,792 --> 00:20:52,793
[PRECIOUS GROANS]

422
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:56,088
Billy…

423
00:20:57,047 --> 00:21:01,385
I know it hurts and it's hard.

424
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,472
But maybe you should talk to him.

425
00:21:07,015 --> 00:21:08,684
Not for his sake,

426
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:12,062
but to finally give yourself some peace.

427
00:21:13,188 --> 00:21:18,735
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

428
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:22,322
[PHONE RINGING]

429
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:23,865
[LINE RINGING]

430
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,660
[PHONE RINGING]

431
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:29,955
[LINE RINGING]

432
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,082
[PHONE RINGING]

433
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:36,628
[LINE DISCONNECTING]

434
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:41,675
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

435
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:42,759
[SIGHS]

436
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:54,604
Let's go.

437
00:21:56,815 --> 00:22:03,822
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

438
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:11,163
<i>Let me be</i>
<i>a mother to you just this once.</i>

439
00:22:11,246 --> 00:22:13,415
[BILLY] <i>It's really hard</i>

440
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:15,792
<i>when you can't escape</i>
<i>the person who hurt you.</i>

441
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:17,169
<i>My father called last night.</i>

442
00:22:17,794 --> 00:22:20,130
<i>You know you can</i>
<i>talk to me.</i>

443
00:22:20,714 --> 00:22:22,257
<i>Anytime, okay?</i>

444
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:25,552
<i>Get used to calling me Abi.</i>
<i>Abi! Abi! Abi! Abi! Abi!</i>

445
00:22:25,635 --> 00:22:27,554
<i>And we shouldn't be</i>
<i>seen together.</i>

446
00:22:27,637 --> 00:22:28,930
<i>It'll be a big problem.</i>

447
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:30,098
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>Family</i>

448
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:31,975
<i>is never meant</i>
<i>to be split up.</i>

449
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:33,560
<i>Oliver's still</i>
<i>with you, right?</i>

450
00:22:33,643 --> 00:22:36,063
<i>- What's wrong?</i>
<i>- Keep an eye on him. Please.</i>

451
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:37,397
[BILLY] <i>Oliver, no!</i>

452
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:38,648
<i>No!</i>
